      "reasons": [
        "The packet uses “variable error” to refer to precision in specific tasks (e.g., “smaller variable error”), but it does not explicitly define variable error as “a measure of how much a person’s responses vary across repeated judgments or tasks,” so that substantive part of the definition is unsupported by the provided text.",
        "Because the packet provides only that smaller variable error corresponds to “better precision,” the definition’s explanation of what variable error directly measures (response variation across repeated judgments/tasks) is an added generalization not supported in the supplied packet."
